(4956145, 717608, 72318, '<td valign="top">Nice idea for the challenge, I think it lacks a bit of impact through a bit too much negative space within the image which might have been a factor on the end result.  Ever seen the film "Strings"? would recommend it if you enjoy the whole concept of puppets...</td>', 'Nice idea for the challenge, I think it lacks a bit of impact through a bit too much negative space within the image which might have been a factor on the end result.  Ever seen the film "Strings"? would recommend it if you enjoy the whole concept of puppets...', '2008-09-15 11:29:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956209, 716354, 76430, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your high finish and personal best. I think it would have done better with a more realistic looking background.  Maybe actually putting the doll in front of the screen rather than printing it out.  <br/> <br/>"Unlikely event"?  Of course I have heard of Labyrinth, but I haven''t seen it nor even seen any excerpt that I can recall and knew nothing of the plot.  As a David Bowie and Sci-Fi fan I should have and will be looking for it at my video store.  It sounds good.</td>', 'Congratulations on your high finish and personal best. I think it would have done better with a more realistic looking background.  Maybe actually putting the doll in front of the screen rather than printing it out.   "Unlikely event"?  Of course I have heard of Labyrinth, but I haven''t seen it nor even seen any excerpt that I can recall and knew nothing of the plot.  As a David Bowie and Sci-Fi fan I should have and will be looking for it at my video store.  It sounds good.', '2008-09-15 12:19:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956655, 717501, 40679, '<td valign="top">Hi, this is a comment from the critique club!<br/> <br/>First of all I want to say that I love the beautiful b/w tones you used here. The high contrast makes it very dramatic. Light looks good.<br/> <br/>Some things I''d change on this one. The composition could''ve been better, maybe a landscape orientated photo with negative space at the left would''ve solved that. Also I''d play around a bit with the broom and doll, but I don''t know what you''ve been trying :)</td>', 'Hi, this is a comment from the critique club! First of all I want to say that I love the beautiful b/w tones you used here. The high contrast makes it very dramatic. Light looks good. Some things I''d change on this one. The composition could''ve been better, maybe a landscape orientated photo with negative space at the left would''ve solved that. Also I''d play around a bit with the broom and doll, but I don''t know what you''ve been trying :)', '2008-09-15 16:19:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956666, 715535, 40679, '<td valign="top">Hi, this is a comment from the critique club! <br/> <br/>That is one beautiful antique doll! And she still looks very good. Well preserved, I guess ;) The colors look good with the subject.<br/> <br/>There are a couple of issues here in my opinion that might have cost you a point. <br/> <br/>- the sharpness / focus isn''t very good. It seems like the eyes aren''t sharp enough *at this resolution* might have sharpened it a little bit more.<br/>- the background is a bit folded. My eyes went there immediately, while you''d rather have the main attention at the doll.<br/>- I miss a very little piece of the dress at the left. If you want to crop off a piece of something, make it a bit bigger, so you can tell you''re sure about your decision.<br/> <br/>Hope this was helpful!</td>', 'Hi, this is a comment from the critique club!  That is one beautiful antique doll! And she still looks very good. Well preserved, I guess ;) The colors look good with the subject. There are a couple of issues here in my opinion that might have cost you a point.  - the sharpness / focus isn''t very good. It seems like the eyes aren''t sharp enough *at this resolution* might have sharpened it a little bit more.- the background is a bit folded. My eyes went there immediately, while you''d rather have the main attention at the doll.- I miss a very little piece of the dress at the left. If you want to crop off a piece of something, make it a bit bigger, so you can tell you''re sure about your decision. Hope this was helpful!', '2008-09-15 16:25:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956674, 716439, 42013, '<td valign="top">Hi from the Critique Club;<br/> <br/>Ha, looks very lifelike, except the hair. Nicely set up, the jean material makes a decent background, could be a sofa. It would be nice if you had a little more DOF but that is just my personal preference...tough to do with a macro style shot. Your lighting is good and it really did make me do a double take when I opened the page.<br/> <br/>Nice placement and you had good comments + a fav. Keep shooting!<br/> <br/>Mark</td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club; Ha, looks very lifelike, except the hair. Nicely set up, the jean material makes a decent background, could be a sofa. It would be nice if you had a little more DOF but that is just my personal preference...tough to do with a macro style shot. Your lighting is good and it really did make me do a double take when I opened the page. Nice placement and you had good comments + a fav. Keep shooting! Mark', '2008-09-15 16:31:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956682, 717732, 40679, '<td valign="top">Hi, this is a comment from the critique club! <br/> <br/>Oh I love the Matryoshka-dolls! I used to play with them when I was little :)<br/> <br/>The small DoF really works in this photo, especially with the different layers of the shells of the dolls. Colors look nice and the light is good. Only thing I might have done different is the alignment of the head of the doll. Because of the DoF you lose the sharpness on the right eye, if you place the doll with the eyes straight to the cam that might have been better. <br/> <br/>Hope this was helpful!</td>', 'Hi, this is a comment from the critique club!  Oh I love the Matryoshka-dolls! I used to play with them when I was little :) The small DoF really works in this photo, especially with the different layers of the shells of the dolls. Colors look nice and the light is good. Only thing I might have done different is the alignment of the head of the doll. Because of the DoF you lose the sharpness on the right eye, if you place the doll with the eyes straight to the cam that might have been better.  Hope this was helpful!', '2008-09-15 16:36:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956764, 716381, 30982, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Hi Katie,<br/> <br/>I see you''ve entered one challenge so far - welcome to DPC!  You''ll find this is a great place to get a lot of very good advice to help you move forward with photography.  In looking over your comments, you''ve already received some excellent advice and suggestions for this particular entry with respect to composition, focus, lighting.  One thing you might want to look at before your next entry is a tutorial on how to size your images to give the most impact within the limits of DPC.  That tutorial is <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">here.</a> <br/> <br/>I do hope you''ll try another challenge!<br/> <br/>If you have any questions or comments about this critique, feel free to send me a Private Message (click on my name to go to my profile page, then click on the Private Message link.)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Hi Katie, I see you''ve entered one challenge so far - welcome to DPC!  You''ll find this is a great place to get a lot of very good advice to help you move forward with photography.  In looking over your comments, you''ve already received some excellent advice and suggestions for this particular entry with respect to composition, focus, lighting.  One thing you might want to look at before your next entry is a tutorial on how to size your images to give the most impact within the limits of DPC.  That tutorial is here.  I do hope you''ll try another challenge! If you have any questions or comments about this critique, feel free to send me a Private Message (click on my name to go to my profile page, then click on the Private Message link.) ', '2008-09-15 17:33:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956779, 716715, 30982, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Heh!  I didn''t vote on this challenge, partly because I was on vacation and didn''t have my usual time on the computer, and partly because of my embarassing score in this challenge.  I did, however, wander through the challenge just to see what was there, and this one totally cracked me up!  So VERY appropriate for a "dolls" challenge in so many ways.  And your description is priceless.  From the ol'' DPC perspective, what got you scorewise were the technicals.  I really do like the choice of focus on the 2nd doll (at least one other commenter did too) but there are those for whom something in the foreground out of focus is distressing (it''s just the way some are, can''t fix it).  A bit of noise, yes.  Might have been really funny to NeatImage them to death to make them look even more like dolls.... heh.  But the noise actually seems to serve a purpose, since they''re already plastic enough, don''t you think?  A final thought - my grandmother always told me to arrange things in odd - 3, 5, 7, etc - rather than even.  Not sure how much difference that makes.  Your arrangement here is good, but were it mine I''d crop a bit off the top to box them in some and to take away a bit of the white fluffy cloudlike thing in the upper right.  You did notice, I hope, that your commenters enjoyed this.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Heh!  I didn''t vote on this challenge, partly because I was on vacation and didn''t have my usual time on the computer, and partly because of my embarassing score in this challenge.  I did, however, wander through the challenge just to see what was there, and this one totally cracked me up!  So VERY appropriate for a "dolls" challenge in so many ways.  And your description is priceless.  From the ol'' DPC perspective, what got you scorewise were the technicals.  I really do like the choice of focus on the 2nd doll (at least one other commenter did too) but there are those for whom something in the foreground out of focus is distressing (it''s just the way some are, can''t fix it).  A bit of noise, yes.  Might have been really funny to NeatImage them to death to make them look even more like dolls.... heh.  But the noise actually seems to serve a purpose, since they''re already plastic enough, don''t you think?  A final thought - my grandmother always told me to arrange things in odd - 3, 5, 7, etc - rather than even.  Not sure how much difference that makes.  Your arrangement here is good, but were it mine I''d crop a bit off the top to box them in some and to take away a bit of the white fluffy cloudlike thing in the upper right.  You did notice, I hope, that your commenters enjoyed this.', '2008-09-15 17:47:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956823, 717652, 45524, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club. How odd the first one I pull from the que is yours. OK here we go<br/> <br/>First things I find that might have hurt the score, the catch lights in the eyes are not equal(is that a fongsphere?) One thing that I might have changed to see the texture of the doll a bit is add some directional light. Bring it from the side and lets see some texture and shadows out of all those stitches and cloth. It might also bring the catchlights higher in the eye and make them more natural. Crop is nice and tight, but a little centered I might have experimented with it a few different crops to see which I liked better rather then centered.<br/> <br/>I like how you desaturated the colors and have the tones nice and warm. Good luck in future challenges.</td>', 'Greetings from the critique club. How odd the first one I pull from the que is yours. OK here we go First things I find that might have hurt the score, the catch lights in the eyes are not equal(is that a fongsphere?) One thing that I might have changed to see the texture of the doll a bit is add some directional light. Bring it from the side and lets see some texture and shadows out of all those stitches and cloth. It might also bring the catchlights higher in the eye and make them more natural. Crop is nice and tight, but a little centered I might have experimented with it a few different crops to see which I liked better rather then centered. I like how you desaturated the colors and have the tones nice and warm. Good luck in future challenges.', '2008-09-15 18:04:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956858, 716631, 52500, '<td valign="top">**Critique Club**<br/> <br/>My first impression of this image when it popped up was "looks pretty good".  Had I voted this one, I probably would have gone along with the crowd and given it a 5.  I''m kinda surprised you got so many 1,2, and 3 votes, but that''s DPC for ya. :)<br/> <br/>First, the likes.  I like the lighting a lot and I think the pose works quite well.  I think the tilt of the head is just perfect.  If I were shooting this (note: these tips might not necessarily increase your score), I would have moved the doll to the left and toward the camera a bit to give the shadow more room and presence in the shot.  I don''t think it looks quite deliberate enough as it is.  The shot feels pretty static as well with the face being almost perfectly centered.<br/> <br/>Some things I think would improve the score:  Get rid of that pesky sensor dust.  Either clean the sensor or clone those bad boys out (which is legal in basic and advanced).  I think it looks sloppy, and I know I (and probably others) vote down for it.  For me, it''s really all about attention to detail.  Also, I agree with one of your comments that it could be a little sharper.<br/> <br/>Overall, I like it.  With a little tweaking, I think the score could have jumped a ways as well.<br/> <br/>Please feel free to PM me if you have any questions or comments.<br/>Thanks,<br/>Nathan</td>', '**Critique Club** My first impression of this image when it popped up was "looks pretty good".  Had I voted this one, I probably would have gone along with the crowd and given it a 5.  I''m kinda surprised you got so many 1,2, and 3 votes, but that''s DPC for ya. :) First, the likes.  I like the lighting a lot and I think the pose works quite well.  I think the tilt of the head is just perfect.  If I were shooting this (note: these tips might not necessarily increase your score), I would have moved the doll to the left and toward the camera a bit to give the shadow more room and presence in the shot.  I don''t think it looks quite deliberate enough as it is.  The shot feels pretty static as well with the face being almost perfectly centered. Some things I think would improve the score:  Get rid of that pesky sensor dust.  Either clean the sensor or clone those bad boys out (which is legal in basic and advanced).  I think it looks sloppy, and I know I (and probably others) vote down for it.  For me, it''s really all about attention to detail.  Also, I agree with one of your comments that it could be a little sharper. Overall, I like it.  With a little tweaking, I think the score could have jumped a ways as well. Please feel free to PM me if you have any questions or comments.Thanks,Nathan', '2008-09-15 18:17:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956863, 717589, 45524, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club. <br/> <br/>First let me say I think you met the challenge, def a doll or puppet, although could be mistaken for a toy instead. Either way I like your subject, very creative lighting, nothing standard about side lighting, maybe just a touch softer would have helped, not sure of your diffuser but maybe try to soften it or make it appear larger then it is. <br/> <br/>I like the background, but I wish you had maybe used a bit of a reflector on camera right so you can fill in the shadows just a touch and give a bit of detail to the left side of subject.<br/>Overall I think you did well. And scored just about where I would have put it.</td>', 'Greetings from the critique club.  First let me say I think you met the challenge, def a doll or puppet, although could be mistaken for a toy instead. Either way I like your subject, very creative lighting, nothing standard about side lighting, maybe just a touch softer would have helped, not sure of your diffuser but maybe try to soften it or make it appear larger then it is.  I like the background, but I wish you had maybe used a bit of a reflector on camera right so you can fill in the shadows just a touch and give a bit of detail to the left side of subject.Overall I think you did well. And scored just about where I would have put it.', '2008-09-15 18:18:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4956913, 717162, 45524, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club. <br/> <br/>What can I say, you placed fifth on your first entry. Very well done. <br/> <br/>There are a few suggestions I could make to the entry. I like the 45 degree side lighting to your subject and the choice of background. I would have however used a bit of fill light or a reflector on camera left to slightly open up those shadows a bit. I also might have shot this from just a bit lower perspective, you might have been able to get a bit of a catch light in the eye a bit better and not been peering down so much on your subject. Overall I dont think you can complain and have done well for your first entry.</td>', 'Greetings from the critique club.  What can I say, you placed fifth on your first entry. Very well done.  There are a few suggestions I could make to the entry. I like the 45 degree side lighting to your subject and the choice of background. I would have however used a bit of fill light or a reflector on camera left to slightly open up those shadows a bit. I also might have shot this from just a bit lower perspective, you might have been able to get a bit of a catch light in the eye a bit better and not been peering down so much on your subject. Overall I dont think you can complain and have done well for your first entry.', '2008-09-15 18:35:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(4957017, 717593, 3936, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Review<br/> <br/>Color Saturation and Hue:  Colors are vivid, saturation is appropriate for the subject, hues are natural.<br/> <br/>Brightness and contrast:  Image could be a little brighter, contrast is good as the blacks are nice and dark.  Lighting is flat though.<br/> <br/>Focus and depth of field:  Depth of field is too shallow.  The washer or seal under the stopper is nice and sharp.  The figure appears soft at the head, and the rest of the image is soft.  A smaller aperature would make the depth of field deeper.<br/> <br/>The wire assembly for opening and closing the bottle really compete with the subject.  For this view, the doll really has to be lazer sharp.  Lighting from the side could help add relief and apparent sharpness to the doll.  Although the area is small, perhaps a small flashlight, torch, or whatever they call them where you live, could be used to form a small spotlight to draw attention to the doll.<br/> <br/>Another approach might be to pull back further yet, and sort of do a play on the whole angels dancing on the head of a pin thing.<br/> <br/>Interesting picture, I''ve never seen a doll this small.</td>', 'Critique Club Review Color Saturation and Hue:  Colors are vivid, saturation is appropriate for the subject, hues are natural. Brightness and contrast:  Image could be a little brighter, contrast is good as the blacks are nice and dark.  Lighting is flat though. Focus and depth of field:  Depth of field is too shallow.  The washer or seal under the stopper is nice and sharp.  The figure appears soft at the head, and the rest of the image is soft.  A smaller aperature would make the depth of field deeper. The wire assembly for opening and closing the bottle really compete with the subject.  For this view, the doll really has to be lazer sharp.  Lighting from the side could help add relief and apparent sharpness to the doll.  Although the area is small, perhaps a small flashlight, torch, or whatever they call them where you live, could be used to form a small spotlight to draw attention to the doll. Another approach might be to pull back further yet, and sort of do a play on the whole angels dancing on the head of a pin thing. Interesting picture, I''ve never seen a doll this small.', '2008-09-15 19:14:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4957247, 717556, 23098, '<td valign="top">Good colors and the title is just right.  Tack sharp. Good work, doc.</td>', 'Good colors and the title is just right.  Tack sharp. Good work, doc.', '2008-09-15 21:54:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4957916, 716370, 67152, '<td valign="top">Charlene - what a great title to complement the feel of the image.  Component wish, I think the image is very solid - the face slightly at angle, the lace and fine work to frame the dolls head, the misplaced hair - but I think it is lacking something.  The black and white conversion seems very flat in my opinion. Maybe a bit of sepia tone to give it an older, used, and forgotten feel.  Also, maybe a slightly different treatment on the composition may have helped.  A more square crop, with focus more directly on the face itself, and lighting (likely from the side) to emphasize the nicks and scratches and neglect that this pretty doll endured.</td>', 'Charlene - what a great title to complement the feel of the image.  Component wish, I think the image is very solid - the face slightly at angle, the lace and fine work to frame the dolls head, the misplaced hair - but I think it is lacking something.  The black and white conversion seems very flat in my opinion. Maybe a bit of sepia tone to give it an older, used, and forgotten feel.  Also, maybe a slightly different treatment on the composition may have helped.  A more square crop, with focus more directly on the face itself, and lighting (likely from the side) to emphasize the nicks and scratches and neglect that this pretty doll endured.', '2008-09-16 12:33:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4958217, 716889, 98041, '<td valign="top">I thought the tears were a really nice touch.</td>', 'I thought the tears were a really nice touch.', '2008-09-16 14:43:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4958221, 717355, 98041, '<td valign="top">Nice idea.</td>', 'Nice idea.', '2008-09-16 14:45:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4958806, 716889, 65035, '<td valign="top">Deb this is so beautiful and it''s about time you got yourself a blue ribbon, huuuuuge congratulations! Dang girl, you even manage to make a doll look emotive.</td>', 'Deb this is so beautiful and it''s about time you got yourself a blue ribbon, huuuuuge congratulations! Dang girl, you even manage to make a doll look emotive.', '2008-09-16 23:30:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4959367, 716370, 30982, '<td valign="top">I like the doll for this shot - I tend to think of dolls as kind of creepy in a way, and this one fits nicely.  I think you already have some good constructive comments.  I''ll echo that there needs to be a bit more detail somehow in the hair, or perhaps a tighter crop to alleviate the large black space formed there.  I do love the choice of B&amp;W, and the bit of lace in the lower left.</td>', 'I like the doll for this shot - I tend to think of dolls as kind of creepy in a way, and this one fits nicely.  I think you already have some good constructive comments.  I''ll echo that there needs to be a bit more detail somehow in the hair, or perhaps a tighter crop to alleviate the large black space formed there.  I do love the choice of B&W, and the bit of lace in the lower left.', '2008-09-17 07:31:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4960444, 716354, 33352, '<td valign="top">Very nice work : regarding the too much color I really like the effect.</td>', 'Very nice work : regarding the too much color I really like the effect.', '2008-09-17 17:58:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4961048, 716370, 44877, '<td valign="top">OMG Charlene, we ended up right next to each other. Your photo is really much better than mine. I love the high contrast and needless to say, the composition is totally awesome. The title is the icing. Interesting that you got a 6.5 from your commenters, but a 5.1 from the overall voters. Should have ended higher... but we all know how that goes. :o)<br/> <br/></td>', 'OMG Charlene, we ended up right next to each other. Your photo is really much better than mine. I love the high contrast and needless to say, the composition is totally awesome. The title is the icing. Interesting that you got a 6.5 from your commenters, but a 5.1 from the overall voters. Should have ended higher... but we all know how that goes. :o) ', '2008-09-18 00:42:00.000000', NULL, 0),
